{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1497212-have-you-used-the-politics-skill-in-your-games-campaigning-as-social-maneuvering","id":1497212,"title":"Have you used the Politics skill in your games? // Campaigning as social maneuvering","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-15T13:57:20-08:00","id":1497212,"title":"Have you used the Politics skill in your games? // Campaigning as social maneuvering","content":"I'm posting this in general to get a broader view, but I'm thinking about a Changeling chronicle that might involve characters interacting with activists and the local government (which may or may not have occult influences). In some ways, the Politics skill is tricky to nail down, so I could use some examples beyond those in the books. I do have a couple in mind:<ul><li>Recruit activists: Presence + Politics, possibly as a Build Equipment action for a temporary organization.</li> <li>Organize non-violent protest: Resolve + Politics</li> </ul><br /> I'm also considering having campaigning resolved as social maneuvering rolled against voting blocks, with Politics being a general informative skill for the task.<ul><li>Determine voting block's Anchors or Aspirations: Wits + Politics.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T14:16:12-08:00","id":1497217,"title":"","content":"I played in a Hunter Chronicle in which the Cell worked for VASCU. We had to roll Manipulation + Politics to file official requests for any Equipment, Merits or Endowments that were outside of the budget allotted for our Cell per mission. In my Mage Chronicles that I ST'd, the players often rolled Intelligence + Politics to remember info about specific members of the Consilium, usually traits such as Path, Order, Legacy, Cabal and Obsessions. Of note is that such rolls didn't reveal the same info as the Occult Skill. Using Politics to remember another Mage's Obsessions simply offers guidelines on potential ways to trade favors and equivalent actions, rather than explaining any lore behind the supernatural phenomena associated with the Obsessions.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you want more concrete examples of what you can get with Politics-focused Social Maneuvering, do consider checking out the guidelines for Order Requisitions in Signs Of Sorcery for Mage 2ed, and my homebrew for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1476711-homebrew-rubber-band-society\"><b>Rubber Band Society</b></a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Organize non-violent protest: Resolve + Politics </div> </div> </div>Resolve is usually meant to defend against unwanted influences on your thoughts. I'd say this is Manipulation + Politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-15-2022, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T19:05:43-08:00","id":1498906,"title":"","content":"That's sounds pretty interesting to discuss. I never thought about it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27685-rutillo","name":"Rutillo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T19:30:43-08:00","id":1499109,"title":"","content":"We used politics a lot for dealing with mortal-society in Masquerade-games. A mortal political-figure was murdered and the player decided to roll politics to investigate who would want him murdered; they DF'd, in front of me; I had to blow it off and had them reroll, but, I kept the first roll and them create a massive conspiracy-theory about who killed them when it was just a random, rogue vampire. <br /> <br /> But, honestly, most political rolls are actually role-played rather than a simple roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}